course: dictionary
lesson: 2108
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Contribute» is a verb, an action word, with three main meanings: to give money, time or help along with other people; to help cause something; and to share an idea in a discussion.
explain: «School reports use formal words: "conscientious" means careful and hard-working, and "contributes enthusiastically" means joins in with energy.» The word «enthusiastically» is your clue. It means with energy and eagerness, so here contribute means to take part and add to something.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «She wants to contribute to the food bank», "give help along with others" fits. In «Smoking contributes to illness», "helps cause" fits, but "gives money" does not. Read the clues, then choose the meaning that makes sense.
fact: «Contribute» means to give money, time or help together with other people.
fact: To contribute to something means to help cause it, as in «Smoking contributes to illness.»
fact: To contribute an idea means to share it in a discussion, such as in class.
fact: «Contributes enthusiastically» means joins in with energy.
fact: Contribute, contributes, contributed and contributing are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «Maya wants to contribute to the food bank.» What does contribute mean here? | Sleep at school | Forget the food bank | Argue with the teacher | *Give help along with others
exercise: «Smoking contributes to illness.» What does contribute mean here? | Stops | Shares a song with | Gives money to | *Helps cause
exercise: In the class discussion, Ravi wants to contribute an idea. What does he do? | Writes a letter to the head teacher | Hides under his desk | *Shares his idea with the group | Tears up his notes
test: «The children contributed £5 each to the class trip.» What does contributed mean here? | Stole the money | Lost their money | Spent all day shopping | *Gave money along with others
test: «He did not contribute a single idea in the discussion.» What does contribute mean here? | Ran away from | *Shared an idea | Hid under the table | Washed
exam: In «contributes enthusiastically», what does enthusiastically mean? | Quietly | Late | Angrily | *With energy and eagerness
